 makes a new file from the template of the rule that governs it

   file <path>       the new file, relative to the repository root wherever the command runs. An
                     absolute path inside the repository is accepted. A path outside it is refused.

   --rule            the rule whose template to use. Default: the most specific rule that governs
                     the path and has templates. A script with no extension needs this flag.

   --variant         the template to use. Default: the first variant the rule lists that the path
                     allows.

   --<hole>=<value>  the value of a hole («name») within a line of the template. The holes path,
                     name, and stem default to values taken from the path. Every other hole needs
                     its flag.


 kit new file
